title: Bound Ethereum receipt proofs with configurable max node size and depth

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Node Dev]
    description: |
      Replaces the unbounded `Vec<Vec<u8>>` receipt proof in Snowbridge's verification
      primitives with bounded types `ReceiptProofNode<MaxNodeSize>` and
      `ReceiptProof<MaxNodeSize, MaxDepth>` backed by `BoundedVec`. This prevents
      attackers from submitting oversized receipt proofs that cause unbounded
      verification work under fixed-weight dispatch calls.

      Two new pallet constants `MaxMptNodeSize` and `MaxReceiptProofDepth` are added
      to `snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client::Config`, with defaults of 32 KiB per node
      and 16 nodes per proof — matching Ethereum receipt trie depth bounds.

      The `Verifier` trait and `Proof`/`EventProof` types are made generic over the
      proof type to support runtime-configured bounds. Inbound and outbound queue
      pallets now include worst-case invalid-proof weights in their submit extrinsics.

      Bridge hub runtimes (westend, rococo) are configured with the default bounds.

crates:
  - name: snowbridge-verification-primitives
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-beacon-primitives
    bump: patch
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-inbound-queue-primitives
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue-v2
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-outbound-queue-v2
    bump: minor
  - name: snowbridge-outbound-queue-primitives
    bump: patch
  - name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: bridge-hub-rococo-runtime
    bump: patch
